#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# key_union

#% text
# `key_union([a1, a2, ...])` gives the associations with every key that any of them has: a key an association lacks is added with the value `missing(key_absent, key)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `key_union(list, f)` gives `f(key)` for an absent key instead.

#% item
# Keys come in order of first appearance; every result has the same keys in the same order.

#% item
# Lists of rules are read as associations.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
key_union([assoc(a -> 1), assoc(b -> 2)])
#% output
#= [assoc(a -> 1, b -> missing("KeyAbsent", b)), assoc(a -> missing("KeyAbsent", a), b -> 2)]

#% text
# A default value for the absent keys:

#% cell
key_union([assoc(a -> 1), assoc(b -> 2)], k => 0)
#% output
#= [assoc(a -> 1, b -> 0), assoc(a -> 0, b -> 2)]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `key_intersection`, `merge`, `join_across`
